  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 16 January 1933; four nominations for four seats, no contest (Irish Weekly and Ulster Examiner, 14 January 1933, p. 10). 'Four nominations were received at Cookstown. They were the four retiring councillors — Messrs. Samuel M'Kinney, W. E. M. Allen, George Ferguson, jun., J. M'Dowell-Scott. There were no other nominations, so there will be no contests.' Returned unopposed."
